XDJ-RX patch 20: high-speed USB on the i.MX6 ChipIdea host (faster track loads).

The front USB slots sit behind a hub on HOST1. Three things kept mass storage slow:
 1. Speed: ChipIdea/TDI EHCI reports the port speed in PORTSC[27:26] (PSPD) and Linux
    (ehci_port_speed when ehci_is_TDI) reads it there; QEMU left it 0, so the hub and
    the stick enumerated as USB 1.1 full speed (12 Mbit/s). The hub (patch 08) also
    never set PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED for its ports. Now: PSPD = 10b for a high-speed
    device, and the hub reports high-speed ports.
 2. With the link at high speed, the BSP's fsl_platform_h1_set_usb_phy_dis() clears
    USBSTS[7] SRI ("SOF received", ChipIdea) and busy-waits for the next SOF -- QEMU
    never set it, so khubd spun forever and the hub never enumerated. SRI now reads 1.
 3. The firmware caps USB requests at 8 KB (usb-iosched.sh), so per-request latency
    rules throughput; each request is CBW -> data -> CSW, and QEMU only notices the
    guest's next qTD on its frame timer (>= 1 ms). While the async schedule is busy
    (5 ms window) a ChipIdea controller now re-polls every microframe (125 us).
Measured (20 MB dd, cache dropped, with patch 21): 1.3 -> 5.6 MB/s; a 60 MB WAV
"fully loaded" (pad progress bar) 10.6 -> 7.4 s. Link 480 Mbit/s, khubd idle.

--- a/hw/usb/chipidea.c
+++ b/hw/usb/chipidea.c
@@ -198,6 +198,16 @@
     sec->capsbase   = 0x100;
     sec->opregbase  = 0x140;
     sec->portnr     = 1;
+    /*
+     * ChipIdea is a TDI-style EHCI with an integrated transaction translator: it
+     * reports the attached device's speed in PORTSC[27:26] (PSPD), and Linux
+     * (ehci_port_speed() when ehci_is_TDI) takes the root-port speed from there.
+     * Without it every root-port device reads as full speed (12 Mbit/s).
+     * It also has USBSTS[7] SRI ("SOF received", set every (micro)frame): the
+     * i.MX6 BSP's fsl_platform_h1_set_usb_phy_dis() clears it and busy-waits for
+     * the next SOF when a high-speed device connects -- never set = khubd spins.
+     */
+    sec->tdi   = true;
 
     set_bit(DEVICE_CATEGORY_USB, dc->categories);
     dc->desc = "Chipidea USB Module";
--- a/hw/usb/dev-hub.c
+++ b/hw/usb/dev-hub.c
@@ -231,6 +231,13 @@
         } else {
             usb_hub_port_clear(port, PORT_STAT_LOW_SPEED);
         }
+        /* A high-speed device on a high-speed hub port (patch 08) must be reported
+         * as such, or the host treats it as full speed (12 Mbit/s) behind a TT. */
+        if (port->port.dev->speed == USB_SPEED_HIGH) {
+            usb_hub_port_set(port, PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED);
+        } else {
+            usb_hub_port_clear(port, PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED);
+        }
     }
     return notify;
 }
